---
layout: null
sitemap: false
---
{% comment %}
  search.json — the search index, built fresh every time the site builds.

  Why it's built here: GitHub Pages has no server to ask questions to.
  So we write every entry and log into one file at build time, and the
  browser downloads it and searches it by itself (see assets/js/search.js).

  Why the comments are only in this Liquid block: Liquid comments vanish
  from the output, so the finished search.json stays pure data. JSON doesn't
  allow comments at all, and a stray one would break the search.

  Why the keys are short ("k", "x"...): this file grows with every entry,
  and short keys keep it small for phones on slow data.
    k = kind ("e" entry or "l" log)   u = link
    x = text                          c = chapter
    g = log title                     d = date
    a = creator                       y = type
    s = status                        tg = tags

  jsonify turns any value into safe JSON (quotes, line breaks and all).
  Tripped me up: a hand-written "{{ value }}" between quotes breaks as soon
  as a post contains a quote mark. Always use jsonify.
{% endcomment %}
[
{%- for log in site.logs -%}
{"k":"l","u":{{ log.url | relative_url | jsonify }},"g":{{ log.title | jsonify }},"a":{{ log.creator | jsonify }},"y":{{ log.type | jsonify }},"s":{{ log.status | jsonify }},"tg":{{ log.tags | jsonify }}},
{%- endfor -%}
{%- assign all_entries = site.entries | sort: "date" | reverse -%}
{%- for e in all_entries -%}
{%- assign parent = site.logs | where: "slug", e.log | first -%}
{%- assign anchor = e.path | split: "/" | last | split: "." | first | prepend: "e-" -%}
{"k":"e","u":{{ parent.url | append: "#" | append: anchor | relative_url | jsonify }},"g":{{ parent.title | default: e.log | jsonify }},"c":{{ e.chapter | jsonify }},"d":{{ e.date | date: "%-d %b %Y" | jsonify }},"x":{{ e.content | strip | jsonify }}}{% unless forloop.last %},{% endunless %}
{%- endfor -%}
]
